# Cloudflare DB + server actions

## Timestamps

Hyperdrive / `node-postgres` may return timestamp columns as **strings**, not `Date`.

- **Never** call `.toISOString()` directly on values from Drizzle `select()` when serializing for server actions, RSC props, or JSON responses.
- **Always** use `toIsoTimestamp()` / `toDate()` from `@acme/db/serialize-timestamp`.
- In Drizzle schema, prefer `t.timestamp({ mode: "date", withTimezone: true })` for columns read in production server code.

## Server-only modules

- Use `import "server-only"` in `*.server.ts` under `lib/blink/`, **not** `"use server"`.
- `"use server"` belongs only in `src/app/actions/*.ts`. Putting it on shared libs forces every export to be an async server action.

## DB client on Workers

- Prefer `getDbAsync()` from `@acme/db/client` in server actions when sync `getCloudflareContext()` fails.
- Avoid circular imports between `admin-roles.server.ts` and `internal-email-grants.server.ts` (keep role lookup in one direction).

## Internal team grants

- Persist DB grant **before** sending Resend email so access is not lost when email fails.
- `RESEND_FROM_EMAIL` must use a domain verified in Resend (e.g. `Blink <no-reply@blinkperps.xyz>`).
